#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Historically, Kadupul administrators created simple Data Input Methods that include commands like \"ps -ef | grep something | wc -l\" to represent a numeric value for use in Kadupul Graphs.  In earlier versions of Kadupul, this was permitted.  However, this is an unsafe practice as it is a gateway for third party users to publish insecure Data Templates.  In modern Kadupul, these types of practices should be avoided.  However, we provide this option if you have older Data Input Methods that contain these unsafe Meta Characters and have not converted them to local scripts in the 'scripts' directory.  When this option is unchecked, Kadupul restricts shell-style metacharacters such as quotation marks, curly brackets, vertical bars, backslashes, and backticks.  Kadupul continues to allow greater-than and less-than signs for things like <path_cacti> and for input parameters, but if this option is unchecked, that is the limit of their permitted use."
msgstr "Histories het Kadupul-administrateurs eenvoudige datainvoermetodes geskep wat opdragte soos \"ps -ef | grep something | wc -l\" insluit om 'n numeriese waarde vir gebruik in Kadupul-grafieke voor te stel. In vroeër weergawes van Kadupul is dit toegelaat. Dit is egter 'n onveilige praktyk omdat dit 'n toegangspoort vir derdepartygebruikers bied om onveilige datasjablone te publiseer. In moderne Kadupul moet hierdie soort praktyke vermy word. Ons bied egter hierdie opsie as jy ouer datainvoermetodes het wat hierdie onveilige metakarakters bevat en dit nog nie na plaaslike skripte in die 'scripts'-gids omgeskakel het nie. Wanneer hierdie opsie nie gemerk is nie, beperk Kadupul dopstyl-metakarakters soos aanhalingstekens, krulhakies, vertikale strepe, terugskuinsskrape en terugtiks. Kadupul laat steeds groter-as- en kleiner-as-tekens toe vir dinge soos <path_cacti> en vir invoerparameters, maar as hierdie opsie nie gemerk is nie, is dit die perk van hul toegelate gebruik."

